#19445
The Geyser~
The steam released by your sharp pick has ripped a jagged hole through
the volcanic tuff and obsidian above and below you.  Unlike the smooth
tunnels carved by the tenticles, you find abundant handholds suitable
for climbing into the hole above your head, or safely descending into
the rumbling abyss below your feet.  You spy two hollows with smooth
walls to the north and west bearing tenticle marks.  You would 
be well-advised to make your explorations hasty, as it is uncertain 
just how long it will take before the geyser repressurizes and 
blows again...
~
