#19446
The Geyser~
As you descend into the geyser hole, you find that your handholds of
volcanic tuff have been replaced with solid bedrock granite.  The crack
below you has irissed itself down so tight that even the smallest
pixie would be unable to squeeze inside it.  You can see now that the
gargolith has left its imprint on these walls, carving smooth rooms
in four directions to safely harbor its young within this hellish world 
of geothermal heat and steam.
~
