#19447
The Geyser~
You have managed to scramble your way up through the volcanic tough
into a small room where presumably a deposit of soluble rock has been
eroded away by the hot steam from below.  The roof of this room is
solid obsidian glass, much harder than the surrounding volcanic tuff,
which has been carved by both gargolith tenticle and steam alike into
a myriad of passageways and rooms.  The geyser hole continues west and
down.
~
