#19448
The Geyser~
The steam from the earth below has found a small seam in the obsidian
glass above your head, carving a small hole which you'd be hard-pressed
to squeeze yourself into, so to speak.  A hint of sunlight from above
lights the acrid air, and you have a sudden yet impractical urge to
claw your way through the solid rock to freedom and fresh air.  All 
around you are the marks of the gargolith, who has carved wide rooms 
in the volcanic tuff to house its young, oddly secure in this hostile
environment.
~
